   "body": "Implemented a focused fork fix: [reveal routing history opened from Usage](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/c931166aadb24c635d4897857da2a0766572e9b3).\n\nBoth Usage routing links (expanded details and the timestamp) now pass the trusted navigation click into `openRoute`. It waits for the view to open, reveals the selected story, then records arrival so asynchronous page loads do not restore the previous off-screen position. It uses the existing purposeful-scroll mechanism; clicking a request within Routing still preserves the reader's position.\n\nVerification:\n- New `usage-routing-visible.test.cjs` starts with a scrolled Routing page, navigates from the actual Usage link and asserts that the selected story header is inside the viewport.\n- It fails against the original assets and passes in Chromium and WebKit for en, zh, zh-TW, ja and de (10 cases).\n- Existing `routing-failed-open.test.cjs` passes in both engines (8 cases), including no page movement when selecting a Routing row.\n- Existing `usage-ledger.test.cjs` was also run in both engines. Its newest-live-route assertions and route-callback cleanup error reproduce on the unchanged upstream base; they are not claimed fixed here.\n\n[Branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/nvidia-parameters-routing) · [Full validation and limitations](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/blob/055637f4dccc2b9a843a52a5456aab3f41fa64f5/VALIDATION.md).\n\nNo new UI strings or production deployment. #3623's broader Usage attempt-history presentation is intentionally left to the maintainer; this patch only makes the existing navigation reveal its destination.",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
